
# Task 08 – Compilation Process

## Aim
To understand the stages of compiling a C program using GCC.

## Compilation Stages

1. Preprocessing
2. Compilation
3. Assembly
4. Linking
5. Execution

## GCC Commands

Preprocessing:
gcc -E billing.c -o billing.i

Generate assembly:
gcc -S billing.c -o billing.s

Generate object file:
gcc -c billing.c -o billing.o

Generate executable:
gcc billing.c -o billing

Run:
./billing

## Conclusion
The GCC compiler converts C source code into an executable program through preprocessing, compilation, assembly and linking.

